(7430672, 1171405, 100393, '<td valign="top">This image has caused me to stop and pay attention. That means it is in my 7-10 voting band. (Voted earlier) <br/> <br/>Additionally, it is highly interesting/eclectic meaning it keeps me here long enough to offer a longer comment and a vote of 8 or more. <br/> <br/>This is one of my 10s - I like it very much. Furthermore I think it enriches the DPC collective portfolio. Put simply, I wish we saw more stuff like this. Let me tell you why it pushes all the right buttons for me: <br/> <br/>1. Fantastic tones<br/>2. The <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_N.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_N.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_N.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=113156" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">jagar</a> characteristic smooth glow / sharpness combo - I haven''t seen that since you moved away from from your Fuji<br/>3. Fantastically engaging subject<br/>4. Really super composition<br/>5. Perfectly judged vignette / edge burn<br/> <br/>Overall this an amazingly image that transports us elsewhere.<br/> <br/>Awarded for the Best of 2015:<br/> <br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=1051747" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/100000-104999/100393/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1051747.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/100000-104999/100393/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1051747.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/100000-104999/100393/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1051747.jpg"/></a></td>', 'This image has caused me to stop and pay attention. That means it is in my 7-10 voting band. (Voted earlier)  Additionally, it is highly interesting/eclectic meaning it keeps me here long enough to offer a longer comment and a vote of 8 or more.  This is one of my 10s - I like it very much. Furthermore I think it enriches the DPC collective portfolio. Put simply, I wish we saw more stuff like this. Let me tell you why it pushes all the right buttons for me:  1. Fantastic tones2. The  jagar characteristic smooth glow / sharpness combo - I haven''t seen that since you moved away from from your Fuji3. Fantastically engaging subject4. Really super composition5. Perfectly judged vignette / edge burn Overall this an amazingly image that transports us elsewhere. Awarded for the Best of 2015: ', '2016-01-21 15:38:23.000000', NULL, 1),
