(7431080, 1172289, 112739, '<td valign="top">I think you got your wish, finishing near the top of the portraits. Congratulations Paul. Excellent.</td>', 'I think you got your wish, finishing near the top of the portraits. Congratulations Paul. Excellent.', '2016-01-22 10:15:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(7431082, 1172702, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the Critique club<br/> <br/>An appealing image that meets the challenge<br/> <br/>Truly an artistic result. I''m sure a lot of patience was needed to get this high standard image of a technically challenging subject, thanks for all the technical detail. The focus is nice and sharp throughout with the action frozen in sharp detail. The colours add to the appeal, the way they have separated with the little yellow fringe is just great. The only thing I can question about it is whether it might have been better to exclude the top drop, I think I would have preferred it without but thats just my personal opinion.<br/> <br/>I''m sure you had a lot of fun doing this if not only from the many different shapes you will have encountered. In any other challenge this would have been on the front page but well done anyway.<br/> <br/></td>', 'Hello from the Critique club An appealing image that meets the challenge Truly an artistic result. I''m sure a lot of patience was needed to get this high standard image of a technically challenging subject, thanks for all the technical detail. The focus is nice and sharp throughout with the action frozen in sharp detail. The colours add to the appeal, the way they have separated with the little yellow fringe is just great. The only thing I can question about it is whether it might have been better to exclude the top drop, I think I would have preferred it without but thats just my personal opinion. I''m sure you had a lot of fun doing this if not only from the many different shapes you will have encountered. In any other challenge this would have been on the front page but well done anyway. ', '2016-01-22 10:25:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(7431083, 1172732, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the Critique club<br/> <br/>An appealing image that meets the challenge<br/> <br/>The Northern lights are a spectacular event to witness and especially to photograph and there have been a lot of amazing examples on DPC over the years. Your image whilst it might not be the most impressive in terms of the aurora itself is nonetheless very pleasing because you have made the effort to compose it using a landscape that would stand on its own merits alone. The foregrounds are often very tricky in this situation but I think you have handed it quite well with sufficient detail to enhance the landscape. The sky and clouds are a spectacular addition but they do dominate the aurora to a somewhat minor entity so reducing its impact a little.<br/> <br/>A great image in a tough challenge, thanks for your entry<br/> <br/></td>', 'Hello from the Critique club An appealing image that meets the challenge The Northern lights are a spectacular event to witness and especially to photograph and there have been a lot of amazing examples on DPC over the years. Your image whilst it might not be the most impressive in terms of the aurora itself is nonetheless very pleasing because you have made the effort to compose it using a landscape that would stand on its own merits alone. The foregrounds are often very tricky in this situation but I think you have handed it quite well with sufficient detail to enhance the landscape. The sky and clouds are a spectacular addition but they do dominate the aurora to a somewhat minor entity so reducing its impact a little. A great image in a tough challenge, thanks for your entry ', '2016-01-22 10:34:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(7431084, 1173884, 53200, '<td valign="top">In My Opinion:<br/>I agree with Lydia about the pacifier.  Also would that sweater(?) she is wearing show her off to better advantage versus the blanket?<br/>I would love to see both her eyes - could you have propped her head on a pillow to get a better view or maybe just taken the photo from a lower angle?<br/>How did this look in color?  Baby colors are usually soft and (to me) they enhance any photo of an infant - it might have made a difference in the voter''s eyes.<br/>Anna is gorgeous - my Annie''s photo (my beloved Cocker Spaniel) is my favorite in my portfolio even though it''s my lowest scoring photo - so I know what you mean about your feelings for this shot.  Hopefully you''ll be able to enter more photos of her in future challenges.<br/></td>', 'In My Opinion:I agree with Lydia about the pacifier.  Also would that sweater(?) she is wearing show her off to better advantage versus the blanket?I would love to see both her eyes - could you have propped her head on a pillow to get a better view or maybe just taken the photo from a lower angle?How did this look in color?  Baby colors are usually soft and (to me) they enhance any photo of an infant - it might have made a difference in the voter''s eyes.Anna is gorgeous - my Annie''s photo (my beloved Cocker Spaniel) is my favorite in my portfolio even though it''s my lowest scoring photo - so I know what you mean about your feelings for this shot.  Hopefully you''ll be able to enter more photos of her in future challenges.', '2016-01-22 10:34:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(7431091, 1173629, 12611, '<td valign="top">Love it. Beautiful motion, emotion, and mystery enough for all. The euphoric feeling of arriving or returning to a backyard picnic or campfire, muddled with a brilliant and blazing urban soul...</td>', 'Love it. Beautiful motion, emotion, and mystery enough for all. The euphoric feeling of arriving or returning to a backyard picnic or campfire, muddled with a brilliant and blazing urban soul...', '2016-01-22 10:57:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(7431092, 1171463, 12611, '<td valign="top">sad little piece of ice- like a snowman a few days after the storm- goodbye little guy...</td>', 'sad little piece of ice- like a snowman a few days after the storm- goodbye little guy...', '2016-01-22 10:59:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(7431094, 1171806, 12611, '<td valign="top">Like Don said, the figures are great. There is a surrealist feel, a feel of Morning, of latent potency and potential, of hope in the future, or at least anticipation as the city awakens.</td>', 'Like Don said, the figures are great. There is a surrealist feel, a feel of Morning, of latent potency and potential, of hope in the future, or at least anticipation as the city awakens.', '2016-01-22 11:01:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(7431101, 1172876, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the Critique club<br/> <br/>An appealing image that meets the challenge<br/> <br/>I can see why this place appeals to you so, it appeals to me too, all those lovely old wooden structures and walkways. I generally like your composition, the river with its reflections an ice shapes is enticing. I like that you have converted it to mono however the tonal range and contrast is somewhat limited, you should have made much better use of the filters to emphasise certain aspects of the image more then others. The one thing that really lets the shot down is the blown sky which in itself is something to be avoided but it is also very dominant in the image overall. I think you could have greatly improved the end result by tilting the camera down to avoid this bright sky so that the you excluded it in preference for more walkway foreground. You would still have had an interesting sky in what was left of it.<br/> <br/>Thank you for your entry in this very demanding challenge <br/> <br/> <br/></td>', 'Hello from the Critique club An appealing image that meets the challenge I can see why this place appeals to you so, it appeals to me too, all those lovely old wooden structures and walkways. I generally like your composition, the river with its reflections an ice shapes is enticing. I like that you have converted it to mono however the tonal range and contrast is somewhat limited, you should have made much better use of the filters to emphasise certain aspects of the image more then others. The one thing that really lets the shot down is the blown sky which in itself is something to be avoided but it is also very dominant in the image overall. I think you could have greatly improved the end result by tilting the camera down to avoid this bright sky so that the you excluded it in preference for more walkway foreground. You would still have had an interesting sky in what was left of it. Thank you for your entry in this very demanding challenge   ', '2016-01-22 11:17:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(7431105, 1173427, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the Critique club<br/> <br/>An appealing image that meets the challenge<br/> <br/>You have given us some of the best aurora shots out there and this is yet another stunning example, well worthy of your high placing. Your choice of foreground interest is key to the additional interest and impact that the shot has. I have to say that I am drawn to the lovely distant mountains on the right and left feeling, I wish your composition had been more off-centre moving the plane to the left with more of the right, I think you would still have retained the most dynamic effects of the aurora but with an even more pleasing composition. <br/> <br/>Thank you for your entry in this very demanding challenge <br/> <br/> <br/></td>', 'Hello from the Critique club An appealing image that meets the challenge You have given us some of the best aurora shots out there and this is yet another stunning example, well worthy of your high placing. Your choice of foreground interest is key to the additional interest and impact that the shot has. I have to say that I am drawn to the lovely distant mountains on the right and left feeling, I wish your composition had been more off-centre moving the plane to the left with more of the right, I think you would still have retained the most dynamic effects of the aurora but with an even more pleasing composition.  Thank you for your entry in this very demanding challenge   ', '2016-01-22 11:47:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(7431108, 1173483, 38032, '<td valign="top">This certainly would have won a ribbon in an appropriate challenge. "Music" for example.</td>', 'This certainly would have won a ribbon in an appropriate challenge. "Music" for example.', '2016-01-22 11:52:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(7431111, 1174041, 102315, '<td valign="top"><a href="//smg.photobucket.com/user/91mini/media/internet%20forum%20pics/lolaverykj8.gif.html" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//img.photobucket.com/albums/v153/91mini/internet%20forum%20pics/lolaverykj8.gif'', strrpos(''//img.photobucket.com/albums/v153/91mini/internet%20forum%20pics/lolaverykj8.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//img.photobucket.com/albums/v153/91mini/internet%20forum%20pics/lolaverykj8.gif"/></a></td>', '', '2016-01-22 11:57:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(7431113, 1173931, 8759, '<td valign="top">awesomeness</td>', 'awesomeness', '2016-01-22 12:04:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(7431114, 1163273, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the Critique club<br/> <br/>An appealing image that meets the challenge<br/> <br/>A lovely landscape scene during the last remains of the ''golden hour''.Your long exposure has resulted in a pleasant mix of detail together with motion smoothness of the waters. I''m a little frustrated that the sunset strip is interrupted on the left as much as it is and left feeling I wish you had moved over to the right a little more, assuming of course that was possible, so there was less of the lower left in favour of more unobstructed sunset. Overall its a very competent landscape of an attractive scene.<br/> <br/>In a less demanding challenge this would undoubtedly have placed higher but well done anyway, thank you for your entry.<br/> <br/> <br/></td>', 'Hello from the Critique club An appealing image that meets the challenge A lovely landscape scene during the last remains of the ''golden hour''.Your long exposure has resulted in a pleasant mix of detail together with motion smoothness of the waters. I''m a little frustrated that the sunset strip is interrupted on the left as much as it is and left feeling I wish you had moved over to the right a little more, assuming of course that was possible, so there was less of the lower left in favour of more unobstructed sunset. Overall its a very competent landscape of an attractive scene. In a less demanding challenge this would undoubtedly have placed higher but well done anyway, thank you for your entry.  ', '2016-01-22 12:07:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(7431116, 1172314, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the Critique club<br/> <br/>An appealing image that meets the challenge<br/> <br/>A lovely portrait of a very attractive lady the shot tells us that she is inextricably linked with the Magnolia public school by placing her between the two coaches together with her clothing. Your lighting and exposure have worked well to make her stand out from the darker background although there are some darker shadows under her chin it is not excessive. Your lower shooting position has enabled you to use more of the sky in a less distracting way than a normal viewpoint. All in all a very competent portrait, well done<br/> <br/>It has been well received in this highly popular challenge, thank you for your entry.<br/> <br/> <br/></td>', 'Hello from the Critique club An appealing image that meets the challenge A lovely portrait of a very attractive lady the shot tells us that she is inextricably linked with the Magnolia public school by placing her between the two coaches together with her clothing. Your lighting and exposure have worked well to make her stand out from the darker background although there are some darker shadows under her chin it is not excessive. Your lower shooting position has enabled you to use more of the sky in a less distracting way than a normal viewpoint. All in all a very competent portrait, well done It has been well received in this highly popular challenge, thank you for your entry.  ', '2016-01-22 12:15:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(7431121, 1172581, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the Critique club<br/> <br/>An appealing image that meets the challenge<br/> <br/>What a lovely old structure that pier is though I''m not sure I would feel too safe in the building! I am intrigued why you seem to have so much noise with such a low setting? I like the combination of near mono together with the muted colours of the building. I think the composition could have been improved by reducing the foreground in favour of the sky which has some interesting detail and texture in it and it would also remove the foreground detail I find rather distracting. The mast is so close to the left edge it should either have more room or have been cropped out. At the other edge the distant beacon is a little too close to the right edge, I think the whole composition would have benefited from a small move to the right.<br/> <br/>A respectable result in such a demanding challenge, well done, thank you for your entry.<br/> <br/> <br/></td>', 'Hello from the Critique club An appealing image that meets the challenge What a lovely old structure that pier is though I''m not sure I would feel too safe in the building! I am intrigued why you seem to have so much noise with such a low setting? I like the combination of near mono together with the muted colours of the building. I think the composition could have been improved by reducing the foreground in favour of the sky which has some interesting detail and texture in it and it would also remove the foreground detail I find rather distracting. The mast is so close to the left edge it should either have more room or have been cropped out. At the other edge the distant beacon is a little too close to the right edge, I think the whole composition would have benefited from a small move to the right. A respectable result in such a demanding challenge, well done, thank you for your entry.  ', '2016-01-22 12:31:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(7431123, 1171806, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the Critique club<br/> <br/>An appealing image that meets the challenge<br/> <br/>There is an air of appealing mystery in your image and spacious minimalism that is created by the broad featureless canal that separates the frenetic detail of the foreground trees and the functional buildings from the really interesting lower left part of the image. This path that recedes into the distance is transformed from a mainly featureless waterside walkway into something intriguing with the inclusion of the figure of the walking man. To a lesser extent the person on the wall adds some more interest but I feel that this would be even stronger if she wasn''t there at all. Your composition and the man''s position is what makes this all such a strong image<br/> <br/>In a less demanding challenge this would have placed even higher, well done, thank you for your entry.<br/> <br/> <br/></td>', 'Hello from the Critique club An appealing image that meets the challenge There is an air of appealing mystery in your image and spacious minimalism that is created by the broad featureless canal that separates the frenetic detail of the foreground trees and the functional buildings from the really interesting lower left part of the image. This path that recedes into the distance is transformed from a mainly featureless waterside walkway into something intriguing with the inclusion of the figure of the walking man. To a lesser extent the person on the wall adds some more interest but I feel that this would be even stronger if she wasn''t there at all. Your composition and the man''s position is what makes this all such a strong image In a less demanding challenge this would have placed even higher, well done, thank you for your entry.  ', '2016-01-22 12:45:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(7431124, 1173868, 50695, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by NiallOTuama:</b></div><hr/><i> Do you own a zebra? </i></td></tr></table>It''s not a zebra and I don''t own it. :)</td>', 'Originally posted by NiallOTuama: Do you own a zebra? It''s not a zebra and I don''t own it. :)', '2016-01-22 12:48:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(7431126, 1168496, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the Critique club<br/> <br/>An appealing image that meets the challenge<br/> <br/>A fascinating street scene, we get to do some people watching from the comfort of our armchair! I like that you have chosen to use mono and done the processing so well, a broad range of tones and detail throughout. There is lots to absorb and hold our interest from foreground shadows to the bench to the shop interior to the man on the left and his surroundings, all very interesting. The only minor criticism I do have is in your title the only person who may possibly be conversing is the lady but his stance is certainly not conducive to such a possibility, perhaps ''street corner observations'' may have been more appropriate?<br/> <br/>In a less demanding challenge this would have placed even higher, well done, thank you for your entry.<br/> <br/> <br/></td>', 'Hello from the Critique club An appealing image that meets the challenge A fascinating street scene, we get to do some people watching from the comfort of our armchair! I like that you have chosen to use mono and done the processing so well, a broad range of tones and detail throughout. There is lots to absorb and hold our interest from foreground shadows to the bench to the shop interior to the man on the left and his surroundings, all very interesting. The only minor criticism I do have is in your title the only person who may possibly be conversing is the lady but his stance is certainly not conducive to such a possibility, perhaps ''street corner observations'' may have been more appropriate? In a less demanding challenge this would have placed even higher, well done, thank you for your entry.  ', '2016-01-22 12:58:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(7431127, 1171222, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the Critique club<br/> <br/>An appealing image that meets the challenge<br/> <br/>The lighting in your landscape has emphasised the undulating nature of the ground producing some lovely shadows giving it all more of a 3D feel. However, I feel the colours have been saturated to the detriment of the overall end result. The strong blue cast especially of the sky and hills also affects the image quality. The white clouds on the right add an interesting counterpoint to the rest of the image<br/> <br/>I''m sorry you didn''t receive any comments during the challenge I hope this makes up for it, well done, thank you for your entry.<br/> <br/> <br/></td>', 'Hello from the Critique club An appealing image that meets the challenge The lighting in your landscape has emphasised the undulating nature of the ground producing some lovely shadows giving it all more of a 3D feel. However, I feel the colours have been saturated to the detriment of the overall end result. The strong blue cast especially of the sky and hills also affects the image quality. The white clouds on the right add an interesting counterpoint to the rest of the image I''m sorry you didn''t receive any comments during the challenge I hope this makes up for it, well done, thank you for your entry.  ', '2016-01-22 13:10:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(7431128, 1169594, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the Critique club<br/> <br/>An appealing image that meets the challenge<br/> <br/>A great and enduring composition with a lot of appeal though the mans gesture with his stick is somewhat ill fitting. I commend your choice of mono and the processing it works very well indeed, this would be nowhere near as effective in colour. My one big issue with the image is the sharpening it has been way overdone, in fact this is the sort of image where none is needed a softer emphasis is more desirable here especially with the atmospheric conditions. It''s a real shame because it does significantly mar the end result. But, well done for seeing and interpreting the scene in the way you have done.<br/> <br/>It shows the quality of this demanding challenge that your 6 has not placed higher, well done, thank you for your entry.<br/> <br/> <br/></td>', 'Hello from the Critique club An appealing image that meets the challenge A great and enduring composition with a lot of appeal though the mans gesture with his stick is somewhat ill fitting. I commend your choice of mono and the processing it works very well indeed, this would be nowhere near as effective in colour. My one big issue with the image is the sharpening it has been way overdone, in fact this is the sort of image where none is needed a softer emphasis is more desirable here especially with the atmospheric conditions. It''s a real shame because it does significantly mar the end result. But, well done for seeing and interpreting the scene in the way you have done. It shows the quality of this demanding challenge that your 6 has not placed higher, well done, thank you for your entry.  ', '2016-01-22 13:20:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(7431130, 1173868, 100831, '<td valign="top">Stripes on stripes... that''s what happened. Sophie must have been amused. I should have commented earlier:(</td>', 'Stripes on stripes... that''s what happened. Sophie must have been amused. I should have commented earlier:(', '2016-01-22 13:29:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(7431131, 1173884, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the Critique club<br/> <br/>An appealing image that meets the challenge<br/> <br/>You could stage manage these sort of shots but what you have here is the sort of image that shows Anna in a way that you can easily imagine and remember her in your unfortunate separation from her. For that reason the dummy becomes acceptable though I do agree it would be nicer to have seen all her features without it. What is vital in any portrait is to get the eyes nice and sharply focused and that''s exactly what you have done and your shallow DOF has placed all the emphasis on that eye which makes it a very effective image. I like the mono processing.<br/> <br/>You have got some good critique from patches and I can understand what he is saying but I actually like it the way it is, but what really matters is that you have a very special image that will always mean so much to you so DPC and scores are really quite secondary.<br/> <br/>Well done, thank you for your entry.<br/> <br/> <br/></td>', 'Hello from the Critique club An appealing image that meets the challenge You could stage manage these sort of shots but what you have here is the sort of image that shows Anna in a way that you can easily imagine and remember her in your unfortunate separation from her. For that reason the dummy becomes acceptable though I do agree it would be nicer to have seen all her features without it. What is vital in any portrait is to get the eyes nice and sharply focused and that''s exactly what you have done and your shallow DOF has placed all the emphasis on that eye which makes it a very effective image. I like the mono processing. You have got some good critique from patches and I can understand what he is saying but I actually like it the way it is, but what really matters is that you have a very special image that will always mean so much to you so DPC and scores are really quite secondary. Well done, thank you for your entry.  ', '2016-01-22 13:33:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(7431138, 1173266, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the Critique club<br/> <br/>An appealing image that meets the challenge<br/> <br/>What an extraordinary bird, very distinctive though your capture is technically sound it just feels rather inanimate as though the bird is stuffed and nailed to the tree. The exposure has worked well for the bird but at the expense of the tree which is significantly overexposed with some loss of detail. I''m sure you have done well to capture this bird, I don''t know how rare it is, your lens suggests that you were quite close to it, but I''m sorry I can''t really get excited about it, it is missing the wow factor.<br/> <br/>Well done, thank you for your entry.<br/> <br/> <br/></td>', 'Hello from the Critique club An appealing image that meets the challenge What an extraordinary bird, very distinctive though your capture is technically sound it just feels rather inanimate as though the bird is stuffed and nailed to the tree. The exposure has worked well for the bird but at the expense of the tree which is significantly overexposed with some loss of detail. I''m sure you have done well to capture this bird, I don''t know how rare it is, your lens suggests that you were quite close to it, but I''m sorry I can''t really get excited about it, it is missing the wow factor. Well done, thank you for your entry.  ', '2016-01-22 13:42:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(7431148, 1171634, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the Critique club<br/> <br/>An appealing image that meets the challenge<br/> <br/>It is always rewarding to capture a natural expression of awe in a candid shot and to that end you have achieved just that here, I just wish that expression had been created by something much more worthy. Your choice of position and composition is excellent. The interior lighting is good but the outside is harsh and overexposed but the most important part, her face, is well exposed and thats what matters most here. I think you could crop the bottom to the level of her red garment for the benefit of the end result.<br/> <br/>Well done, thank you for your entry.<br/></td>', 'Hello from the Critique club An appealing image that meets the challenge It is always rewarding to capture a natural expression of awe in a candid shot and to that end you have achieved just that here, I just wish that expression had been created by something much more worthy. Your choice of position and composition is excellent. The interior lighting is good but the outside is harsh and overexposed but the most important part, her face, is well exposed and thats what matters most here. I think you could crop the bottom to the level of her red garment for the benefit of the end result. Well done, thank you for your entry.', '2016-01-22 13:53:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(7431151, 1173109, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the Critique club<br/> <br/>An appealing image that meets the challenge<br/> <br/>Technically a great shot very well captured, everything is good the detail, the diagonal frame filling composition, the DOF with good sharpness throughout, its difficult to fault, technically. However, I know I am probably in a minority here but I miss any sense of motion that such sharply captured images fail to portray, I need something much more dynamic, some blur in the wingtips from a slower shutter speed or a blurring from a panning shot with a much slower shutter speed, anything that gives me the same sense of freedom that this bird is experiencing would be far more appealing to me. I reiterate there''s no doubt you are skilled in what you are doing here.<br/> <br/>Well done, thank you for your entry.<br/></td>', 'Hello from the Critique club An appealing image that meets the challenge Technically a great shot very well captured, everything is good the detail, the diagonal frame filling composition, the DOF with good sharpness throughout, its difficult to fault, technically. However, I know I am probably in a minority here but I miss any sense of motion that such sharply captured images fail to portray, I need something much more dynamic, some blur in the wingtips from a slower shutter speed or a blurring from a panning shot with a much slower shutter speed, anything that gives me the same sense of freedom that this bird is experiencing would be far more appealing to me. I reiterate there''s no doubt you are skilled in what you are doing here. Well done, thank you for your entry.', '2016-01-22 14:05:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(7431154, 1171655, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the Critique club<br/> <br/>An appealing image that meets the challenge<br/> <br/>At first I thought this was the same image as you won your yellow with Marcel, which effectively it is but a slightly different version. I can understand why you would want to do this given your previous success but these sort of challenges are in themselves very challenging and best met with an image that you consider to be your best as opposed to a DPC most successful. This image lacks the impact of your other in terms of processing, the mono tones and contrast are too limited. The image rotation of your other created an illusion and interest that is sadly lacking here. I think you could have tried something a bit more creative with a panoramic crop of the lower half of the shot with a much brighter background with burnt in shadows which would have given you something very different, perhaps you might try it and see what you think?<br/> <br/>Well done, thank you for your entry.<br/></td>', 'Hello from the Critique club An appealing image that meets the challenge At first I thought this was the same image as you won your yellow with Marcel, which effectively it is but a slightly different version. I can understand why you would want to do this given your previous success but these sort of challenges are in themselves very challenging and best met with an image that you consider to be your best as opposed to a DPC most successful. This image lacks the impact of your other in terms of processing, the mono tones and contrast are too limited. The image rotation of your other created an illusion and interest that is sadly lacking here. I think you could have tried something a bit more creative with a panoramic crop of the lower half of the shot with a much brighter background with burnt in shadows which would have given you something very different, perhaps you might try it and see what you think? Well done, thank you for your entry.', '2016-01-22 14:32:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(7431160, 1171463, 68504, '<td valign="top">like an icy sapphire, rumbling, tumbling. we (southerners) know it''s real but still we don''t believe.</td>', 'like an icy sapphire, rumbling, tumbling. we (southerners) know it''s real but still we don''t believe.', '2016-01-22 14:57:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(7431163, 1172857, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the Critique club<br/> <br/>An appealing image that meets the challenge<br/> <br/>A very impressive landscape Janine, made even more impressive by the lovely lighting. The water and its lovely reflection make a good foreground point of interest. What a lovely sky you have to complete the effect, however, the upper right feels quite empty in relation to the rest of the frame and I wonder whether a panoramic crop just above the mountains may have improved the end result? It''s the nature of this demanding challenge that your image didn''t finish higher but it remains a very competent and appealing landscape.<br/> <br/>Well done, thank you for your entry.<br/></td>', 'Hello from the Critique club An appealing image that meets the challenge A very impressive landscape Janine, made even more impressive by the lovely lighting. The water and its lovely reflection make a good foreground point of interest. What a lovely sky you have to complete the effect, however, the upper right feels quite empty in relation to the rest of the frame and I wonder whether a panoramic crop just above the mountains may have improved the end result? It''s the nature of this demanding challenge that your image didn''t finish higher but it remains a very competent and appealing landscape. Well done, thank you for your entry.', '2016-01-22 15:02:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(7431164, 1173994, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the Critique club<br/> <br/>An appealing image that meets the challenge<br/> <br/>A very impressive aurora landscape. Your choice of viewpoint has made effective use of the mountain backdrop together with the beach foreground to create additional interest. The obvious crowning glory of your shot is the aurora itself a truly impressive spectacle that you have captured well. Its quite uncanny the way the aurora has mimicked the shape of the mountains. In any other challenge this would have won but you have a well deserved front page position.<br/> <br/>Well done, thank you for your entry.<br/></td>', 'Hello from the Critique club An appealing image that meets the challenge A very impressive aurora landscape. Your choice of viewpoint has made effective use of the mountain backdrop together with the beach foreground to create additional interest. The obvious crowning glory of your shot is the aurora itself a truly impressive spectacle that you have captured well. Its quite uncanny the way the aurora has mimicked the shape of the mountains. In any other challenge this would have won but you have a well deserved front page position. Well done, thank you for your entry.', '2016-01-22 15:09:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(7431165, 1169077, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the Critique club<br/> <br/>An appealing image that meets the challenge<br/> <br/>A lovely golden image that has a natural appeal, although it feels somewhat overexposed it suits the nature of the image well. The shallow DOF works well. The ladybird is the obvious focal point for the image and that is where I have a problem. I wish you had composed it more off-centre to the left, I also wish you had completely excluded the distracting sky, so I would suggest a crop just to the right of the furthest tendrils of the ladybird''s stalk and just below the lowest point of the sky, I think this would make a big difference to your end result.<br/> <br/>Well done, thank you for your entry.<br/></td>', 'Hello from the Critique club An appealing image that meets the challenge A lovely golden image that has a natural appeal, although it feels somewhat overexposed it suits the nature of the image well. The shallow DOF works well. The ladybird is the obvious focal point for the image and that is where I have a problem. I wish you had composed it more off-centre to the left, I also wish you had completely excluded the distracting sky, so I would suggest a crop just to the right of the furthest tendrils of the ladybird''s stalk and just below the lowest point of the sky, I think this would make a big difference to your end result. Well done, thank you for your entry.', '2016-01-22 15:16:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(7431170, 1173335, 14476, '<td valign="top">A beautiful image.  Glad to see it did well.</td>', 'A beautiful image.  Glad to see it did well.', '2016-01-22 16:11:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(7431171, 1172888, 14476, '<td valign="top">I wondered who had been to this famous spot recently (or during the past year).  <br/>Love the way you got the waves in silky action.<br/>And, I''m delighted to see that you still sometimes find time to play on DPC, Mark.<br/>:)<br/></td>', 'I wondered who had been to this famous spot recently (or during the past year).  Love the way you got the waves in silky action.And, I''m delighted to see that you still sometimes find time to play on DPC, Mark.:)', '2016-01-22 16:14:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(7431174, 1173512, 30982, '<td valign="top">Pleased to see this did well!</td>', 'Pleased to see this did well!', '2016-01-22 16:41:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(7431181, 1173921, 131419, '<td valign="top">Congratulations, best in the comp in my view, just stunning<br/></td>', 'Congratulations, best in the comp in my view, just stunning', '2016-01-22 17:49:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(7431188, 1173921, 19825, '<td valign="top">This is terrific. It was one of my top scores in the challenge -- sorry I failed to get back and comment earlier. I don''t want to hear any more "I am not very good with portrait stuff" nonsense. We do not see many <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=109227" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">grahamgator</a> portraits, but the occasional ones we get of your husband and others are very good. Keep it up.</td>', 'This is terrific. It was one of my top scores in the challenge -- sorry I failed to get back and comment earlier. I don''t want to hear any more "I am not very good with portrait stuff" nonsense. We do not see many  grahamgator portraits, but the occasional ones we get of your husband and others are very good. Keep it up.', '2016-01-22 18:20:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(7431189, 1172959, 19825, '<td valign="top">This was my top score. Do me a favor, enter more often. Great stuff.</td>', 'This was my top score. Do me a favor, enter more often. Great stuff.', '2016-01-22 18:25:03.000000', NULL, 0),
